{"name":"Allure","hex":"#7291b4","fetched":"2026-10-20","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"allure","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The power to attract, entice; the quality causing attraction."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To entice; to attract."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/allure"}],"entries":[{"title":"Interpersonal attraction","blocks":[{"text":"Interpersonal attraction, as a part of social psychology, is the study of the attraction between people which leads to the development of platonic or romantic relationships. It is distinct from perceptions such as physical attractiveness, and involves views of what is and what is not considered beautiful or attractive."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interpersonal_attraction","wikidata":"Q2632514"},{"title":"Seduction","blocks":[{"text":"In sexuality, seduction means enticing someone else into sexual intercourse or other sexual activity. Strategies of seduction include conversation and sexual scripts, paralingual features, non-verbal communication, and short-term behavioural strategies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_The_Proposal_%281872%29.jpg/330px-William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_The_Proposal_%281872%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seduction","wikidata":"Q1527023"},{"title":"Allure (magazine)","blocks":[{"text":"Allure is an American women's fashion beauty magazine, published monthly by Condé Nast in New York City. It was founded in 1991 by Linda Wells. Michelle Lee replaced Wells in 2015. A signature of the magazine is its annual Best of Beauty awards—accolades given in the October issue to beauty products deemed the best by Allure's staff."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/08/Allure_magazine_30th_anniversary_issue_March_2021.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allure_(magazine)","wikidata":"Q370099"},{"title":"Allure (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Allure is the debut studio album by American girl group Allure. It was released by Crave Records on May 6, 1997 in the United States."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7c/Allureallure.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allure_(album)","wikidata":"Q4733349"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_The_Proposal_%281872%29.jpg/500px-William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_The_Proposal_%281872%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_The_Proposal_%281872%29.jpg/500px-William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_The_Proposal_%281872%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Proposal (1872), William-Adolphe Bouguereau (1825–1905)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWilliam-Adolphe_Bouguereau_(1825-1905)_-_The_Proposal_(1872).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Delila_schert_Simson_die_Haare.jpg/500px-Delila_schert_Simson_die_Haare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Delila_schert_Simson_die_Haare.jpg/500px-Delila_schert_Simson_die_Haare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Delilah cutting Samson's hair, c. 1460","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADelila_schert_Simson_die_Haare.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/The_Dark_Triad_Image.png/330px-The_Dark_Triad_Image.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&u